Freeze the vendored mbedTLS tree: never self-update at configure time.

Upstream pico_keys_sdk_import.cmake probes pico-keys-sdk/mbedtls with
git and, when the checkout differs from its expected ref (v3.6.6 with
the default options), silently fetches from the network, deletes
mbedtls/framework, and checks out that ref. That configure-time
self-mutation makes the effective mbedTLS input differ from the
declared submodule pin (3.6.2, commit 107ea89d) and requires
build-time network access.

P11Lab freezes the effective input directly (mbedTLS v3.6.6,
0bebf8b8, plus its framework sub-tree) as hash-sealed vendored
archives, so the self-update block must not run: with no .git
metadata the tag probe fails, NEED_UPDATE would read ON, and cmake
would attempt a network fetch (silently ignored) and delete the
frozen framework directory. This patch forces NEED_UPDATE OFF with
an explanatory status line. The built library sources are exactly
the frozen v3.6.6 tree, i.e. what the reference network build
produces after its silent upgrade. Build-freeze provisioning
extension, not a semantic change: no compiled source, flag, or
firmware behavior changes.

P11Lab-authored for the opensc-pico provider recipe.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
Applies to pico-keys-sdk at
44ee0254165d6338e27e6739c19c648f83b5c6c9 (shared across both
OpenSC channels).

--- a/pico_keys_sdk_import.cmake
+++ b/pico_keys_sdk_import.cmake
@@ -179,6 +179,13 @@
         endif()
 
     endif()
+
+    # P11Lab: frozen vendored sources are authoritative. Never probe,
+    # fetch, delete, or check out mbedTLS inputs at configure time; the
+    # pinned v3.6.6 tree (the ref this block would otherwise enforce) is
+    # used exactly as vendored.
+    message(STATUS "P11Lab: using frozen vendored mbedTLS, self-update disabled")
+    set(NEED_UPDATE OFF)
 
     if(NEED_UPDATE)
         message(STATUS "Updating mbedTLS source code...")
